However, you might have come across a bit too strong.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: What do you mean? Was this when people were asking questions?<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Yes. If you will correct them constantly, you may not only interrupt their train of thought but it also affects their confidence.", "id": 2, "time": "25000", "image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I guess ... I'll never know what they were thinking. Unless ... I hand out a survey!<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: If you will hand out a survey, you must be prepared for both positive and negative feedback.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I ought to just ask people what they thought in person.<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Hmm ... if you will keep up with that, you must have a chat with Denise.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I should just give up then!<br><span class=\"strong\">Leonard</span>: Don't do that. If you won't put time and effort into this, you must expect no one else will.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: That's true and I won't have accomplished what I set out to do!", "id": 3, "time": "72600", "image": "engenn10le15ob05re2img06.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}